      "summary": "The page size is read from `/proc/self/auxv` at startup rather than assumed. RSS is a count of pages multiplied by it, so a hardcoded 4096 reports every process at a quarter of its real memory on a 16 KiB-page kernel and a sixteenth on a 64 KiB one — Asahi and RHEL aarch64 respectively — and nothing about the output looks wrong. Where the kernel will not say, poptop assumes 4096 and says that it did.",
